{
  "exp_id": "EXP-2",
  "title": "Medium dataset: where a single node gives out",
  "hypothesis": "As the data grows, the single-node pandas configuration (B2) is the first to fail; B3 and P finish where it fails; P stays within 20% of B3's time.",
  "independent_variable": "dataset size (customers), configuration",
  "dependent_measures": [
    "completed",
    "wall_clock_s",
    "peak_rss_mb",
    "bytes_on_disk",
    "rows_trained",
    "test_pr_auc",
    "p_to_b3_time_ratio",
    "validation_gates_s"
  ],
  "started_at": "2026-10-11T18:04:25.350694+00:00",
  "duration_s": 9017.16,
  "status": "partial",
  "hypothesis_held": false,
  "conclusion": "Ladder: 400 customers, 0.4 MB on disk: B2 ok in 12s, B3 ok in 75s; 1500 customers, 1.4 MB on disk: B2 ok in 12s, B3 ok in 68s; 6000 customers, 5.1 MB on disk: B2 ok in 9s, B3 ok in 82s; 20000 customers, 14.9 MB on disk: B2 ok in 34s, B3 ok in 119s; 50000 customers, 36.4 MB on disk: B2 ok in 45s, B3 ok in 180s; 100000 customers, 76.3 MB on disk: B2 ok in 118s, B3 ok in 332s; 200000 customers, 153.9 MB on disk: B2 FAILED in 19s, B3 ok in 509s. Crossover observed at customers_200000: the single-node pandas configuration failed while the Spark configuration completed, which is the shape the hypothesis asserts. At the largest rung both completed (customers_100000), B2 took 117.7s and B3 331.7s, with peak memory 2326.5 MB for B2's Python process and 2134.4 MB for B3's Spark JVM. P at customers_200000 did not finish: stopped at ESCALATED: feature job failed. The PRD's 10 GB tier is not reported: see the limitations.",
  "limitations": [
    "REES46 monthly files were not used: they are not available in this environment, and the PRD asks for them only 'where available'.",
    "The ladder stopped at 200000 customers, where B2 failed and B3 succeeded. Rungs above that were not run: the crossover is the measurement, and pushing both to failure adds nothing.",
    "The PRD's 10 GB tier was not run. At 769 bytes per customer on disk (customers_200000), 10 GB is about 14.0 million customers, and at this run's generation rate that is about 18 hours of generation alone, by a generator that holds each table in memory before writing it, in a 3 GB container (ADR-0002). That extrapolates the generator only; no result is estimated for that size. What is measured instead is the crossover the hypothesis asserts, and P beside B3 where it happens."
  ],
